### 3 Track selection and electron identification

#### Track selection

Electron (including positron if not specified) candidates are selected from good tracks satisfied the flowing selection:

1. number of fit points (_nHitsFit_) in the TPC greater than 19 ( maximum 45) to ensure good tracking quality and momentum resolution;
2. the ratio of number of fit points over number of possible fit points in TPC greater than 0.52 to avoid split tracks in the TPC;
3. distance of closet approach (_dca_) to the primary vertex less then 1 cm to make sure selected tracks are from the primary collision;
4. number of _dE/dx_ points used for calculation average _dE/dx_ greater than 15 to ensure good _dE/dx_ resolution.

